From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drjit-core: do not include <immintrin.h> on riscv64

A scikit-build build takes Dr.Jit's headers from the installed drjit wheel,
but src/python/CMakeLists.txt also adds the vendored ext/drjit include
directories with -I to every Python extension target, so those copies win
over the wheel's -isystem ones. drjit-core/intrin.h assumes "not aarch64"
means x86 and includes <immintrin.h>:

    fatal error: immintrin.h: No such file or directory

This is the same hunk as patches/drjit/1.5.0/0001 applied to the drjit
wheel this build links against, so the vendored and installed headers stay
identical. Every intrinsic gated behind this header is itself gated behind
a compiler-predefined macro (__F16C__, __AVX__, ...) never defined on
riscv64.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; belongs in mitsuba-renderer/drjit-core together with the drjit riscv64 fix, then picked up here through the ext/drjit submodule]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/ext/drjit/ext/drjit-core/include/drjit-core/intrin.h b/ext/drjit/ext/drjit-core/include/drjit-core/intrin.h
--- a/ext/drjit/ext/drjit-core/include/drjit-core/intrin.h
+++ b/ext/drjit/ext/drjit-core/include/drjit-core/intrin.h
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 #  if defined(__aarch64__)
 #    include <arm_neon.h>
 #    include <arm_fp16.h>
+#  elif !defined(__i386__) && !defined(__x86_64__)
+    // Neither x86 nor aarch64: no intrinsics header needed. Every intrinsic
+    // gated behind this header is itself gated behind a real compiler flag
+    // macro (__F16C__, __AVX__, etc.) that is never defined here.
 #  elif !defined(DRJIT_DISABLE_AVX512) || !defined(__AVX512F__)
 #    include <immintrin.h>
 #  else
